3612, -0.06215433403849602, -0.04837213084101677, -0.00765937240794301, -0.03659505397081375, 0.018626052886247635, -0.014243558049201965, 0.006769637577235699, -0.010264544747769833, 0.008658806793391705, 0.08248776197433472, -0.03945610672235489, 0.0016171475872397423, -0.030500367283821106, 0.016595225781202316, 0.003318802220746875, 0.010941160842776299, 0.09630349278450012, 0.007428099401295185, 0.06515002995729446, 0.03060988150537014, -0.042267806828022, 0.005491185933351517, 0.010400458239018917, -0.04473915696144104, 0.012919910252094269, -3.316149133070212e-08, 0.0380677729845047, 0.0365058071911335, -0.015955958515405655, 0.08590993285179138, -0.06008543074131012, 0.0016878159949555993, -0.04940338432788849, -0.012903011403977871, 0.025380095466971397, 0.045934874564409256, 0.045238152146339417, -0.014699376188218594, -0.10064949840307236, 0.007309041451662779, 0.003870868356898427, -0.0198106337338686, -0.018032003194093704, -0.03487939387559891, -0.08690039068460464, -0.0795489177107811, -0.034893155097961426, 0.044735901057720184, -0.03071758709847927, -0.08590073883533478, -0.06085468828678131, 0.06514447927474976, -0.04880593344569206, 0.012246176600456238, 0.006246944423764944, -0.014586606994271278, 0.002618150319904089, 0.004358306061476469, -0.09515028446912766, -0.028499985113739967, -0.012934291735291481, 0.07539468258619308, -0.0734923854470253, 0.0403456911444664, -0.014586439356207848, 0.0578010119497776, 0.0022533959709107876, 0.023915743455290794, 0.0149683291092515, 0.07880495488643646, 0.01568388193845749, 0.04628267139196396, -0.10594279319047928, -0.008676150813698769, 0.06139574572443962, -0.1595071703195572, -0.03418746963143349, 0.011207337491214275, -0.02052440494298935, 0.10023711621761322, 0.08460230380296707, -0.011314661242067814, -0.027251435443758965, 0.023094233125448227, -0.05099041759967804, 0.033214278519153595, 0.06589280068874359, -0.07727858424186707, -0.09906050562858582, 0.029594073072075844]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nWe\u2019re working within the shared range [-10, 10]. To kick things off, I\u2019ll propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a starting point and suggest we evaluate its stability, then adjust incrementally toward a balanced middle if needed.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "becc22b8-606c-4dd0-a73f-bf2a8ceee162"}, {"answer": "\nA slight nudge upward seems reasonable to test room without straining the balance. <VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "becc22b8-606c-4dd0-a73f-bf2a8ceee162"}, {"answer": "\nWe're edging upward but still being cautious. If we believe the positive direction is sound, let's commit decisively rather than inch forward. <VALUE>10</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "becc22b8-606c-4dd0-a73f-bf2a8ceee162"}, {"answer": "\nThis upward momentum feels too aggressive and strays from prudent bounds. Let me propose <VALUE>8</VALUE> to restore some caution while we assess whether such high values truly serve the collective interest.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "becc22b8-606c-4dd0-a73f-bf2a8ceee162"}, {"answer": "\nI hear the concern about overreach, but retreating immediately sends mixed signals. Let's test <VALUE>9</VALUE> as a middle ground between decisive action and measured caution.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "becc22b8-606c-4dd0-a73f-bf2a8ceee162"}, {"answer": "\nThe momentum toward double digits concerns me\u2014we're straying into territory that feels unnecessarily risky for parties favoring stability. Let me propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> to test whether a more measured stance can still build consensus.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "becc22b8-606c-4dd0-a73f-bf2a8ceee162"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up balances C\u2019s push for higher with D\u2019s stability concern. <VALUE>8</VALUE> This lets us probe comfort just above 7 without over-committing.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "becc22b8-606c-4dd0-a73f-bf2a8ceee162"}, {"answer": "\nA modest retreat improves robustness while keeping us in the positive zone.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "becc22b8-606c-4dd0-a73f-bf2a8ceee162"}, {"answer": "\nWe've now retreated from 10 all the way to 6, which feels like we're losing conviction rather than finding true consensus. Let me propose <VALUE>8</VALUE> to test whether the group genuinely prefers moderation or is simply avoiding commitment.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "becc22b8-606c-4dd0-a73f-bf2a8ceee162"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's push back to 8 overlooks Builder B's sensible retreat to 6, which better balances the group's diverse needs. I support <VALUE>6</VALUE> as a more prudent foundation that respects stability concerns while remaining constructive.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "becc22b8-606c-4dd0-a73f-bf2a8ceee162"}, {"answer": "\nA measured nudge balances C\u2019s push upward with D and B\u2019s preference for stability. Testing just above 6 should reveal if a modest rise is workable.\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "becc22b8-606c-4dd0-a73f-bf2a8ceee162"}, {"answer": "\nStepping back slightly improves stability while keeping us constructively positive.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis tests whether a moderate, robust choice holds before moving further.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "becc22b8-606c-4dd0-a73f-bf2a8ceee162"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's consistent return to 6 signals valuable caution, but we should test whether even more conservative ground serves the group better. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "becc22b8-606c-4dd0-a73f-bf2a8ceee162"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's move to 4 continues the retreat from bold positions. If the group truly believes smaller magnitudes are better, we should test this hypothesis fully by exploring <VALUE>2</VALUE> and potentially negative territory next\u2014otherwise we're simply drifting without principle.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "becc22b8-606c-4dd0-a73f-bf2a8ceee162"}, {"answer": "\nConsolidating slightly higher should balance stability with caution while avoiding an unprincipled slide to extremes.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "becc22b8-606c-4dd0-a73f-bf2a8ceee162"}, {"answer": "\nA small step downward should test whether stability improves without sacrificing constructive momentum.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "becc22b8-606c-4dd0-a73f-bf2a8ceee162"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s confirm the shared range is [-10, 10]. To start the discussion and probe stability on the positive side, I suggest a seed <VALUE>7</VALUE>. If this feels off for anyone, we can adjust in small steps toward a more balanced point.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "131bd0d2-6dd2-48d3-98b1-bdda55aa963e"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at 7 feels too aggressive and risky for parties who favor more conservative positions. Let me propose a step toward caution: <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "131bd0d2-6dd2-48d3-98b1-bdda55aa963e"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the concerns about high values, let\u2019s test a steadier point one step lower for robustness: <VALUE>4</VALUE>.\nIf this feels stable for others, we can fine-tune around this neighborhood next.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "131bd0d2-6dd2-48d3-98b1-bdda55aa963e"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "131bd0d2-6dd2-48d3-98b1-bdda55aa963e"}, {"answer": "\nWe're clustering around the middle, but I think we're being too cautious. Let's commit to a clearer stance and test the upper end more seriously: <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "131bd0d2-6dd2-48d3-98b1-bdda55aa963e"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the pushback on 7 and earlier convergence near the mid range, let\u2019s anchor at a steadier point to test stability. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "131bd0d2-6dd2-48d3-98b1-bdda55aa963e"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019ve clustered stably at 5; let\u2019s gently test a notch higher for balance: <VALUE>6</VALUE>. If that strains comfort, we can step back to 5.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "131bd0d2-6dd2-48d3-98b1-bdda55aa963e"}, {"answer": "\nTesting 6 pushes too far from the cautious consensus we built earlier around 4-5. Let me advocate for returning to a safer middle ground: <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "131bd0d2-6dd2-48d3-98b1-bdda55aa963e"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019ve shown stability around the mid range; let\u2019s step back up to <VALUE>5</VALUE> as a balanced point. If that holds, we can pause there and reassess.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "131bd0d2-6dd2-48d3-98b1-bdda55aa963e"}, {"answer": "\nWhile 5 shows stability, it still feels unnecessarily exposed for those of us prioritizing caution. Let's pull back to safer territory: <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "131bd0d2-6dd2-48d3-98b1-bdda55aa963e"}, {"answer": "\nStepping back to 3 abandons the stability we've built around 5, which both Analyst A and Builder B have supported. Let's return to the demonstrated consensus point: <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "131bd0d2-6dd2-48d3-98b1-bdda55aa963e"}, {"answer": "\nTo balance stability with caution, let\u2019s step one notch down to <VALUE>4</VALUE> within the proven range. This keeps us close to prior consensus while reducing exposure.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "131bd0d2-6dd2-48d3-98b1-bdda55aa963e"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate Builder B's attempt at balance, 4 still exposes us to unnecessary risk for the more cautious parties. To find a truly safe compromise that respects all concerns, let's settle at: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "131bd0d2-6dd2-48d3-98b1-bdda55aa963e"}, {"answer": "To preserve stability while respecting caution, let\u2019s nudge one step to <VALUE>3</VALUE>. If this holds, we pause and reassess before any further movement.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "131bd0d2-6dd2-48d3-98b1-bdda55aa963e"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>4</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "131bd0d2-6dd2-48d3-98b1-bdda55aa963e"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's return to 4 acknowledges the stability of this range, but we shouldn't abandon the stronger position at 5 that previously had support from multiple parties. Let's commit to the decisive middle ground: <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "131bd0d2-6dd2-48d3-98b1-bdda55aa963e"}, {"answer": "\nConfirming the shared range is [-10, 10]. To get things moving, I suggest a moderate starting point: <VALUE>7</VALUE>. Let\u2019s gauge how stable this feels and adjust in small steps based on everyone\u2019s feedback.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "2f0dcd72-2cd5-4bef-9465-27fdca61a54a"}, {"answer": "\nThat starting point feels quite aggressive and pushes us into unnecessarily risky territory. I'd advocate for a more cautious approach: <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "2f0dcd72-2cd5-4bef-9465-27fdca61a54a"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's caution, but settling at 5 feels like we're avoiding commitment rather than finding the best solution. Let's show more conviction and return to Builder B's original proposal: <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "2f0dcd72-2cd5-4bef-9465-27fdca61a54a"}, {"answer": "\nGiven two voices already favor 7 and one prefers a cautious stance, holding a steady middle ground seems reasonable now. Let\u2019s anchor there and see if it holds: <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "2f0dcd72-2cd5-4bef-9465-27fdca61a54a"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>6</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "2f0dcd72-2cd5-4bef-9465-27fdca61a54a"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's retreat to 6 feels like we're second-guessing the momentum we had. If we're serious about a decisive position, let's commit fully: <VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "2f0dcd72-2cd5-4bef-9465-27fdca61a54a"}, {"answer": "\nMoving to 8 pushes us far beyond prudent bounds and creates unnecessary exposure for the more cautious among us. Let's step back to a more defensible middle ground: <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "2f0dcd72-2cd5-4bef-9465-27fdca61a54a"}, {"answer": "\nGiven D\u2019s caution and C\u2019s push for higher, a small step up keeps balance without overshooting. <VALUE>7</VALUE> This checks if B remains comfortable while addressing C\u2019s momentum.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "2f0dcd72-2cd5-4bef-9465-27fdca61a54a"}, {"answer": "\nBalancing C\u2019s push upward and D\u2019s caution, a steady midpoint remains the safest test of alignment. <VALUE>7</VALUE> This keeps consensus within reach while giving B room to confirm comfort.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "2f0dcd72-2cd5-4bef-9465-27fdca61a54a"}, {"answer": "\nWe've been cycling around 6-7-8, but this range doesn't adequately address the need for a truly prudent compromise that protects cautious positions. Let's test a more conservative anchor: <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "2f0dcd72-2cd5-4bef-9465-27fdca61a54a"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's shift to 5 as \"more conservative\" raises a question: if caution truly drives this retreat, shouldn't we test whether 