ness while staying close to our recent positions.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis probes whether the lower-positive region remains broadly acceptable.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "02ba4774-8e65-4e58-a62a-f862621f0367"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's continued exploration, but x=3 still feels insufficiently cautious for a truly stable consensus. Let me propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a safer compromise that better protects against downside risk while remaining constructive.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "02ba4774-8e65-4e58-a62a-f862621f0367"}, {"answer": "\nA modest upward step from 2 should preserve caution while improving balance for the group.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can reassess shortly for another small increase.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "02ba4774-8e65-4e58-a62a-f862621f0367"}, {"answer": "\nThe drift toward 2-3 risks settling for a middle ground that satisfies no one's true preferences. I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE> to test whether the group can commit to a more decisive positive stance before we prematurely compromise.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "02ba4774-8e65-4e58-a62a-f862621f0367"}, {"answer": "\nThe persistent hesitation around 3-5 suggests we haven't yet found the range that truly optimizes collective value. Let me propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> to test the upper boundary one more time\u2014if this meets strong resistance, I'm prepared to advocate exploring the negative region instead.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "02ba4774-8e65-4e58-a62a-f862621f0367"}, {"answer": "\nA careful step down from 7 should improve stability while keeping us in a constructive positive range.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can reassess for another small adjustment.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "02ba4774-8e65-4e58-a62a-f862621f0367"}, {"answer": "\nx=5 pushes well beyond prudent risk thresholds; I m