able baseline that multiple sides have already tolerated; if this is acceptable, we can later test a minimal uptick to validate headroom without overexposing risk.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "ef95fb9e-ef44-475e-9d99-0550e886de3f"}, {"answer": "\nMost have tolerated the current baseline; a cautious, incremental uptick will help test headroom while keeping risk low. Proposing <VALUE>3</VALUE> to gauge comfort before any further moves.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "ef95fb9e-ef44-475e-9d99-0550e886de3f"}, {"answer": "\nThe group oscillates between 2 and 3 without conviction\u2014let's push the boundary decisively and see if bolder commitment creates clarity or genuine objection. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "ef95fb9e-ef44-475e-9d99-0550e886de3f"}, {"answer": "\nA moderate retreat increases the chance of consensus while still preserving some upward intent. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "ef95fb9e-ef44-475e-9d99-0550e886de3f"}, {"answer": "\nWe achieved meaningful convergence at x=2 with Builder B's support; pushing beyond that threshold introduces risk that outweighs marginal gains and threatens our ability to close. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "ef95fb9e-ef44-475e-9d99-0550e886de3f"}, {"answer": "\nLocking at this stable baseline maximizes consensus now while maintaining robustness. <VALUE>2</VALUE> If accepted, we can later run a small, controlled uptick to validate headroom without destabilizing the agreement.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "ef95fb9e-ef44-475e-9d99-0550e886de3f"}, {"answer": "\nThe coalition has anchored firmly at 2, but we've never tested the middle ground between that safe harbor and my earlier ambitious 5. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "ef95fb9e-ef44-475e-9d99-0550e886de3f"}]}